-- examples/checks/asks-refused.rofl — A CONE NEVER ANSWERS A WORLD THAT IS REFUSED.
-- Each asks-refused-*.rofl beside this file asks a relation whose cone reads nothing that refuses, in a world whose
-- other rules make the whole program refused: a function's promise broken, a count under well_founded, a recursion
-- through a negation. Each is refused with its asks as without them. This world, the control, answers its ask.
asks(ra_a).
edb(ra_src).
ra_src(1).
ra_a(X) :- ra_src(X).
ra_b(X) :- ra_src(X), not ra_a(X).
-- expect-row: ra_a[main](1)
